Park Selkies' two key-handling loops while no key or gamepad is held.

Applied at build time by build/patch-selkies.sh; the build fails if any hunk doesn't apply
exactly (git apply: no fuzz, only line offsets). Research: docs/research/14-selkies-idle.md.

Why: WebRTCInput._key_stale_sweep (every 100 ms) and _key_repeat_loop (every 20 ms) start
with the server and poll forever, connected or not: about 60 of the container's ~68 idle
wakeups a second. With nothing held, both loop bodies are no-ops. The patch keeps their
interval sleep but then parks them on an asyncio.Event while nothing is held. Held state
(pressed_keys, gamepad_heartbeats, key_repeat_state, and key_suspended, which needs a
pressed key) is only ever added while handling a client message, so on_message sets the
event once each message is handled.

When this stops applying: re-read the two loops and on_message in the new
selkies/input_handler.py, check that held state is still only added from client messages,
and regenerate the patch against the new file. Drop it once upstream stops polling idle.

diff --git a/selkies/input_handler.py b/selkies/input_handler.py
